==================================================
1. API DESIGN PRINCIPLES
==================================================

Design the API using consistent REST conventions.

Use a versioned API base path such as:

/api/v1

Recommend the final convention.

Use resource-oriented endpoints.

Avoid action-heavy URLs where a resource or state-transition endpoint is clearer.

Examples:

Preferred:

GET /api/v1/students/me

GET /api/v1/homework

POST /api/v1/leave-requests

POST /api/v1/report-cards/{reportCardId}/approvals

Not preferred:

GET /getStudentData

POST /doApproveReportCard

POST /updateEverything

Use:

- JSON request and response bodies
- ISO-8601 date/time formats
- Consistent pagination
- Consistent sorting
- Consistent filtering
- Consistent errors
- Consistent validation messages
- Correlation/request identifiers
- Idempotency where required

