2. MULTI-TENANT API RULE
==================================================

For normal school users, do NOT design APIs that trust arbitrary schoolId values supplied by the browser.

Avoid normal endpoints such as:

GET /api/v1/students?schoolId=123

if the authenticated identity already determines the school.

Preferred concept:

GET /api/v1/students

The backend determines:

Authenticated User
        ↓
School/Tenant Context
        ↓
Role and Permission
        ↓
Authorized Resource Scope
        ↓
Response

Platform Admin APIs may explicitly reference tenant/school identifiers when managing tenants.

Clearly separate:

School-scoped APIs

from:

Platform Admin APIs

